# Prettier owns CODE formatting. It does not own PROSE.
#
# ── Markdown ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Measured, not assumed: running Prettier over architecture/ rewrites all fifteen
# documents. The cause is not proseWrap — it is Markdown TABLE PADDING. Prettier
# pads every cell to the column width, so a table whose cells hold sentences
# produces source lines of several hundred characters. Two consequences, both
# bad: the source becomes unreadable in an editor, and every later edit to one
# cell reflows the whole table, so the diff no longer shows what changed.
#
# These documents are read and reviewed by humans, and their line structure is
# authorial: a line per clause is what makes a prose diff reviewable. That is a
# deliberate scope boundary, not an oversight — see code-conventions.md 5.1.
**/*.md

# ── Not ours to reformat ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The five mockups: the source of truth, reproduced as they are, not rewritten
# (README section 3). Also ESLint-ignored, for the same reason.
prototypes/
# The handoff dossier: corrected in place, but not ours to restyle.
docs/

# ── Generated or machine-owned ────────────────────────────────────────────────
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/generated/
.turbo/
node_modules/

# ── Owned by the emitter, not by the formatter ────────────────────────────────
# These two documents are the TARGET that @arthome/contracts must emit, and the
# moment of truth for that package is `contracts:emit` producing an EMPTY DIFF
# against them. That makes their byte-level formatting a property of the
# emitter, not of the formatter: if Prettier restyles them, the emitter has to
# learn to reproduce Prettier's YAML style or the diff is never empty.
#
# Written after a repository-wide `prettier --write` reflowed storefront.yaml
# while it was being translated, moving every held line number by up to 835 and
# destroying 151 keys. Recovered in full — see the commit. The formatting was
# never the point; the ownership is.
openapi/
